# nr-exthost-jssyntax: new crate mixdog-jssyntax (native/core/crates/mixdog-jssyntax), written; not yet a workspace member.

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace] members: add the line (alphabetical, after "crates/mixdog-js")
    "crates/mixdog-jssyntax",

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace.dependencies]
Internal crates block, after the `mixdog-js = ...` line:
    mixdog-jssyntax = { path = "crates/mixdog-jssyntax" }
External block (next to `regress = "0.10"`):
    tree-sitter = "0.27"                 # mixdog-jssyntax (mixdog-graph keeps its own `tree-sitter = "0.27"` line)
    tree-sitter-javascript = "0.25"      # mixdog-jssyntax: the grammar of the classic-script check
    unicode-ident = "1"                  # mixdog-jssyntax: ID_Start/ID_Continue of identifiers (already in Cargo.lock, 1.0.27)
Cargo.lock resolves with the existing entries only (tree-sitter 0.27.1, tree-sitter-javascript 0.25.0, regress 0.10.5,
unicode-ident 1.0.27); the only new lock change is the `mixdog-jssyntax` package entry (dependencies: regress, tree-sitter,
tree-sitter-javascript, unicode-ident; dev: serde_json).

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing: mixdog-jssyntax does not depend on the hack crate (mixdog-js does not either).

## 4. Consumer (the shell tool's hoist), not part of this task
mixdog-tools exec/hoist.rs `ExtSyntax` (a `syntax.check` pool call) is replaced by the nr-exthost-* wiring task: it calls
`mixdog_jssyntax::check_commonjs_script(&wrapped).is_ok()` on the same wrapper string, and `mixdog-exthost` src/syntax.rs
`check_syntax` plus the worker's `syntax.check` handler (src/ext-host/methods.mjs `syntaxCheck`) go with it. That edge
(`mixdog-tools -> mixdog-jssyntax`) is a Cargo.toml line of a hot file (mixdog-tools/Cargo.toml), written by that task's fragment.
No SERVICE_PENDING name is involved.

## 5. Fixture set index
native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json `sets`: after `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-syntax-cases.mjs --tree <tree>` has
written native/core/fixtures/syntax-cases/MANIFEST.json (the recording itself, cases.json, is committed here), add the set's row
the way verify-manifests.mjs expects.

## 6. Verify (after 1-2)
cargo nextest run -p mixdog-jssyntax --offline
cargo clippy -p mixdog-jssyntax --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings
